/-!
# ECDSA reference test vectors (secp256k1 / secp256r1)

Validates `Lampe.Crypto.Secp256k1.verifyBytes` and
`Lampe.Crypto.Secp256r1.verifyBytes` against vectors generated with
the pure-Python `ecdsa` library, which implements RFC 6979
deterministic signing — so the vectors regenerate identically.

Each curve gets two valid signatures (different keys and messages) and
one tampered signature (a single bit flipped) that must be rejected.

Regenerate with `scripts/gen/secp256k1_ref.py` / `scripts/gen/secp256r1_ref.py`.
-/

namespace Tests.Ecdsa

